From e7b3c588e0131cea84e40a1c46631fe211de26d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:00:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ss3ds: wild weather by type and Pokedex lore behaviours
 (0304)

Hook 0110 block, same Alive wild Pokemon gate, no new toggle, nothing saved (per-slot statics cleared when a slot
empties and on map change):
- Weather picks from the map's own table: fire types stay in out of the rain, ice types come out in snow, electric
  types in a thunderstorm (with little sparks and livelier hops), fire types a bit more on clear days.
- Hoothoot/Noctowl hoot on the hour at night (a visible one hops; otherwise one out of sight if the route has them).
- Abra teleports away when it notices the player (up to twice), flickering out and back in a few tiles off.
- Diglett/Dugtrio sink into the ground and pop up elsewhere (up to three times).
- Sudowoodo stands stock still and silent while the player is within 4 tiles.
- Slowpoke sits at the water's edge dangling its tail for a long while, with small rings.
- Jigglypuff sometimes sings (notes); land wilds within 4 tiles fall asleep.
- Ditto spawns looking like the player's lead and drops the disguise within 2 tiles.
Logs: "weather brings out", "hoots", "teleports away", "digs underground", "pretends to be a tree", "dangles its tail",
"Jigglypuff's song", "Ditto is disguised", "disguise drops".
